1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:06,780
Whenever my grandmother made coffee,
she always set out one extra cup.

2
00:00:07,950 --> 00:00:13,700
If we were three, four cups. If we
were four, five.

3
00:00:14,617 --> 00:00:18,527
“Grandmother, whose is this one?” I
asked her.

4
00:00:20,450 --> 00:00:24,940
She smiled and said, “It is for the
one still on the road.”

5
00:00:26,283 --> 00:00:31,673
For many years, that cup sat empty.

6
00:00:32,950 --> 00:00:36,810
But one rainy evening, there was a
knock at the door.

7
00:00:37,950 --> 00:00:42,810
It was a traveller, soaked by the
rain. Without even asking his name,

8
00:00:42,810 --> 00:00:44,500
she gave him the coffee.

9
00:00:45,450 --> 00:00:49,460
“It is people who fill a house,” she
used to say.

10
00:00:51,283 --> 00:00:57,553
Today she is gone, and I live far from
home.

11
00:00:58,783 --> 00:01:04,223
But when I make coffee, I still set
out one extra cup.

12
00:01:05,450 --> 00:01:10,530
Perhaps the one still on the road is
you.
